{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "PreOperator",
  "description": "`Pre` in a right-hand side (esm-spec \u00a75.1 gives it a meaning of its own only in an event affect): Pre(x) there is x, so its derivative is d[x] (spec \u00a73.2), never 0, and it is lowered to x before differentiation, so no emitted coefficient carries a Pre. Pre of an indexed array state inside a faq body, Pre of a scalar state read by every cell, Pre of one cell read by a scalar equation, a state read both through Pre and directly, nonlinear Pre reads (Pre(b)*a[i], exp(Pre(b))*Pre(a[2])), a read that cancels only once Pre is lowered (Pre(b)*b - b*b), and whole-array Pre at array level (D(c) = -k*Pre(c) + 0.3*Pre(a))."
 },
